<title>UK: CU shares dip after new business figures.</title>
<headline>CU shares dip after new business figures.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Britain's Commercial Union Plc dipped on Wednesday after the insurance group posted new business figures for 1996.</p>
<p>The shares were down 3-1/2p at 712p by 0910 GMT.</p>
<p>Commercial Union said single premium sales rose 20 percent in 1996 to 2.36 billion stg while new annual premiums were up 22 percent at 253 million stg.</p>
<p>&quot;The figures are slightly better than the market expected,&quot; said Tom Bennett, insurance analyst at Paribas Capital Markets.</p>
</text>
